    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability successfully. The ASan report confirms a heap-buffer-overflow READ of size 1 in `mg_mqtt_next_prop` at `mqtt.c:210`, exactly where `prop->id = i[0]` reads past the 10-byte buffer.\n\nThe 10-byte MQTT v5 PUBLISH packet works by declaring a `CORRELATION_DATA` binary property with length 4 but only providing 2 bytes of actual data. This causes `mg_mqtt_next_prop` to advance `ofs` beyond the buffer, and on the next iteration the `prop->id = i[0]` read at line 209 executes before the bounds check at line 211.",
